  "about": "Step 24.2 (design-steward 7.8.12, 7.8.12a piece 4): the one media-types table. A file's type is decided by its first bytes (the signatures below, in this order), never by a name or a declared mime; anything else is refused `type`. Read by the steward host's media library (lib/media.mjs) and by the backend (core/media_types.py). limits.call_body_bytes is the steward gateway's request body bound (api/steward_gateway.py MAX_BODY), which media_call checks its base64 against before calling. The pdf_* limits are read_document's (design-steward 7.8.12b, part 6): pages per call with page images and text-only, page images per turn (an owner turn, a group turn), and characters per page and per call. Office documents, archives and executables are deliberately absent (v1).",
